WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
and hopefully drive additional upsides. So I think that's a great story. And I would say also in

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:11.880
2027, we have a number of readouts, important readouts as well. Avalastimab in stroke

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:21.000
prevention, we will have as well the IELTS, no, we'll have as well the COSIMTA data as well as

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.840
some other phase two readouts as well as starting to read out as well our immune reset portfolio.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:32.240
So I think a number of readouts coming that could further bolster the long-term out.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:39.660
Very clear. Thank you very much. Thank you. Your next question comes from the line of

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.300
Kerry Holford from Barenburg. Please go ahead.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.480
Thank you. A question for me on PluVicto, please. So following the recent European filing withdrawal

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:57.100
in that pre-taxing setting, just keen to hear whether you plan to run any additional trials

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:04.460
to address the EMA requirements. And if not, does the lack of a pre-taxing approval in that

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.580
region have any impact on your peak sales forecast for that drug?

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.040
Yeah, thanks, Kerry. So no impact on the peak sales forecast. We continue to expect $5 billion

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:22.260
plus. We had assumed all along that navigating the European feedback on the comparator arm would be

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:27.800
a challenge. We evaluated multiple ways to try to address it, and we tried to make the best

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.620
arguments that we could. But ultimately, we thought it was prudent at that point to withdraw.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.980
We do see continued strong uptake in the vision population in Europe. It's important to note as

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:45.020
well in Japan and in China, we are able to both have the PSMA4 and PSMA vision,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.440
which are critical, you know, long-term markets. And the next step now for Europe will be the

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.360
hormone-sensitive setting where we, because PluVicto is used in combination with an ARPI

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.760
versus an ARPI, there the comparator arm is what EMA would want. And I think would allow us then

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.900
if we're to move forward now, we have the strong, as you know, RPFS data. We're waiting on the OS

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.080
data. Once we have that OS data, we should be able to file in Europe and then expand the patient

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.020
population there. So I think that was the last question. I think that was the last question.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.480
Well, best outcome, we decided rather than running additional studies, it would take many years

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.120
to just withdraw the file and wait for the HSPC readout.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.260
Lovely. Thank you.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:32.320
Thank you. Your next question today comes from the line of Steve Scaler from TD

